TEST-ONLY FIXTURE. This 512-bit RSA PUBLIC key is intentionally far too small.
It exists so irp-client-protocol.test.ts can check that a key which cannot encrypt
the IRP sign-in request is refused as a key problem. Never use it for anything else.
It is a public key only: the matching private half was discarded, and nothing in
this repository needs it (the test only expects encryption to be refused).
